Yes. Geography wouldn’t merely change the characters in religion; it would change the fundamental metaphors available for understanding existence. And for another animal, the body itself becomes geography.

We shouldn’t assume animals would invent person-shaped gods—or even separate “natural” from “supernatural.” Their religions might be enacted patterns: migrations, scent boundaries, synchronized movement, inherited routes, death rituals, or relationships with forces they can perceive but cannot control.

Here are the most interesting possibilities.

